WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.700
More civilian

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.401
casualties to

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.702
report following a Russian

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.838
missile attacks overnight.

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:05.772
At least three lives

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:07.841
lost in southern city of Odessa

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.376
and another three killed

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:11.511
in the eastern Donetsk region.

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:12.846
Meanwhile, the Ukrainian military

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:14.981
is claiming further territorial gains

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.316
in separate area.

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:17.517
And that's what we find.

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:18.551
Fred Pleitgen.

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:20.253
Fred, I believe he's been spending time

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:21.054
with some of the troops

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:21.888
on the front line.

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:25.492
How are they doing in house morale?

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:26.593
Hi there, Julia.

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:28.228
Well,
it certainly is going for the

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:28.895
for the Ukrainians.

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:29.496
They are saying that

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:30.030
they are making

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.798
territorial gains on some places

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:33.266
in the front lines, specifically

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:34.701
the area where we were

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:35.101
where they said

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:36.202
that they managed to take back

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:37.303
a couple of villages there.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:38.071
But they also say that

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:39.672
the going is extremely tough.

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:40.974
They're able to move forward.

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:42.242
But the Russians are putting up

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:44.210
massive and very stiff resistance

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.378
using artillery

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:46.980
and using combat jets as well.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:47.781
Here's what we witnessed.

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:50.984
Ukrainian forces firing

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:51.918
at Russian troops

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:54.721
holed up in block Adana in south Ukraine.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:55.989
This video, the brigade

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:56.489
says,

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:57.590
shows the Russians

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.793
making a final stand here.

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:01.761
Much of the area near the front lines

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:04.164
deeply scarred by combat.

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:05.498
This is the area of Ukraine

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:06.733
where the heaviest fighting

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.001
is currently taking place.

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:09.436
And you can see what it's done

00:01:09.436 --> 00:01:11.371
to a lot of the buildings in these cities

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:13.239
and villages around this area.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.041
And that fighting is set to get

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.376
even worse

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:19.779
We're with the 68th Yeager Brigade,

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:21.147
which has been making important

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:22.048
gains here.

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:22.782
The soldiers

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:25.085
confident and grateful for U.S.

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:27.087
supply gear

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:29.022
but a lot of the times

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:30.590
it's saved my life, he says.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.691
It saves our lives

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.359
every day from shrapnel,

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:34.661
shelling and bullets.

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:36.196
But some of the

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:37.831
vehicles have already been lost,

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:39.933
and the Russians continue to fire back

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.701
constant artillery shelling

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:44.270
and even airstrikes too close for comfort

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.974
as our crew had to duck for cover

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:12.265
Still, the deputy brigade

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:13.900
commander says his soldiers

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.301
are just getting started.

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:17.637
our counterattack

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:19.772
will definitely be successful, he says.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.174
We believe in victory.

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:23.343
We are moving forward towards our goal.

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:25.445
We are advancing

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:26.946
on this part of the frontline.

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.081
The Ukrainians believe

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:29.382
they have the gear.

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:31.651
The manpower and the determination

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:32.385
to advance

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:36.156
far into Russian held territory.

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:37.557
So as you can see, Julia,

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:38.625
some pretty tough battles

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:39.592
that are going on there

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:40.560
on that southern front

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.428
and in southeastern Ukraine.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:43.696
And of course, we were only on

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:45.165
one small part of that front.

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:47.433
It really is several hundred miles long.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:48.134
And there are areas,

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:49.035
of course, where the going is

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:49.802
even tougher

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.871
for the Ukrainians, where late last week

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.473
the Russians claimed to have shot down

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:55.408
a lot of Western supplied armor.

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:57.010
They're also putting out some videos.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.045
So the going is definitely tough

00:02:59.045 --> 00:02:59.879
for the Ukrainians.

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:01.080
But what really stood out to us,

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.182
Julia, was the fact

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:03.650
that morale was very high

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:04.951
among those Ukrainian soldiers,

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.052
especially after

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:06.686
they've been able

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:08.388
to make those initial gains.

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:09.822
And those gains are very important.

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.491
They go pretty deep into the territory

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:13.459
that has been held by the Russians.

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:14.694
But I think that the Ukrainians

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:16.029
also very much understand

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:17.463
that the going is only going

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:18.998
to get tougher from here on.

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:20.466
The Russians have very strong

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:22.902
layers, defenses in the hinterland.

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:25.705
Those go on for a very large part

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:27.740
or for a very long distance.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.509
And the Ukrainians know that the Russians

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:30.710
have some pretty tough soldiers

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.278
down there on the ground as well.

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:34.847
So nobody expecting that this offensive

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:35.782
is going to be quick,

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:36.649
that it's going to be short

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:37.650
or that it's going to be easy.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:37.984
In fact,

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:39.686
the Ukrainians say they understand

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:41.854
if anything, things are going to be long

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:43.823
and things are going to get even tougher

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:44.557
than they already are.

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:46.693
Julia Yeah, they're prepared.

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:47.794
Fred, good to have you.

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:49.529
Thank you. Fred Pleitgen there.

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:51.197
Partial success.

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:51.965
Those are the words

00:03:51.965 --> 00:03:53.132
Ukraine is using today

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.701
to describe intense ground

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:56.436
fighting in the opening phase

00:03:56.436 --> 00:03:58.471
of its summer counteroffensive.

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:01.341
Advances are reported in Bermuda

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:02.675
and separately.

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:03.910
By all accounts,

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:06.079
fighting has been intense.

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:07.714
And these battles are happening

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:10.717
amid increasing air attacks by Russia.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.252
Ukraine says missile

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:14.320
strikes killed three people in Odessa.

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:17.090
And three others in the Donetsk region.

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:18.591
I want to bring in our senior

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:19.692
international correspondent

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:22.595
Sam Collier joins us now live from Kiev.

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:24.230
Good to have you with us.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:24.964
So let's start

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:27.100
with this summit counteroffensive

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.268
certainly underway.

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:29.936
Talk to us about where the efforts

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:30.970
are focused right now.

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:34.707
Well, I think the main

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:35.642
new effort,

00:04:35.642 --> 00:04:37.176
if you like, is on that

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:37.977
front line in

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:38.745
is Aparicio

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:40.113
basically about halfway

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:42.849
between Zachary's city and Donetsk

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:45.451
the latter, of course, held by

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:46.653
Russian backed separatists

00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:48.288
since 20, 14, 15.

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:49.922
So in that context,

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:51.424
this is a very important

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:51.958
front line

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:53.793
indeed from the Russian perspective

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:55.995
because it is the defensive line

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:56.763
against possible

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:58.131
Ukrainian advances

00:04:58.131 --> 00:05:00.600
towards relief of the Crimean peninsula.

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:01.567
It's also

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:04.170
captured by Russia back in 2014.

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:07.340
But the Ukrainians initially began

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.876
with their results there in a rather

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:11.644
low level

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:13.646
a series of reconnaissance raids

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:15.014
reconnaissance by forces

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:17.150
is known in the military right now.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.319
It's stepped up its actions

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:20.853
in a significant way.

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:22.922
It's still not a kind of blitzkrieg

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:24.824
it's not the massive assault

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:26.759
that many people were anticipating.

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:27.627
They're still

00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:30.530
making very small incremental gains here

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:30.863
and there.

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:33.633
They are taking significant casualties

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.468
of the scale of those casualties,

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:37.870
of course, remain a military secret.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.138
But we have seen evidence

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:39.806
that they've lost

00:05:39.806 --> 00:05:41.307
some of the NATO's equipment,

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:43.042
inevitably, that they were going

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:44.177
that they were given

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:46.846
to use in this counteroffensive.

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:48.681
But, Linda, at the same time,

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:50.383
they are enjoying success

00:05:50.383 --> 00:05:52.051
and gaining momentum

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:53.586
in a salient of territory

00:05:53.586 --> 00:05:55.621
south of the city of Parma.

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:56.689
Now, that puts

00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:57.623
the Russian troops

00:05:57.623 --> 00:05:58.725
that have been battling there

00:05:58.725 --> 00:06:00.593
for more than a year

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:01.260
in a very,

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.061
very brutal

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:05.264
and ongoing struggle on the back foot.

00:06:05.298 --> 00:06:06.933
That is an important development

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:07.767
because of the way

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:08.501
it will

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:10.770
split the pressure on the Russians

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:11.971
making it difficult

00:06:11.971 --> 00:06:13.406
for the Russian commanders

00:06:13.406 --> 00:06:14.440
to decide quite

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:15.942
where to invest their troops.

00:06:15.942 --> 00:06:16.709
But they do

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:18.878
still have the advantage, the Russians,

00:06:19.112 --> 00:06:20.079
in terms of troop

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:21.781
troop numbers, in terms of the fact

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:23.883
that they can dominate the skies

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:24.450
above all.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:25.718
And it's for that reason

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:27.320
that the Ukrainians are continuing

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:29.322
to make international pleas

00:06:29.322 --> 00:06:30.323
for the help

00:06:30.323 --> 00:06:32.692
with particularly F-16 aircraft.

00:06:32.692 --> 00:06:34.093
There are a number of countries

00:06:34.093 --> 00:06:35.695
that are currently agreeing

00:06:35.695 --> 00:06:37.730
to have agreed to or even begun

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:40.400
training of pilots on fourth generation

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:41.534
fighter jets.

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:42.935
But they've yet to be seen.

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:43.870
Any of those jets

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:46.439
given are much less deployed here

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:47.907
in Ukraine Linda.

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:50.243
And I'm speaking about additional

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:51.477
military aid the U.S.

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:54.480
has indicated that more aid is coming in

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:57.216
the form of additional armored vehicles.

00:06:57.650 --> 00:06:58.050
And this,

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:58.785
of course, comes

00:06:58.785 --> 00:07:01.421
as the head of Russia's private

00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:02.855
military company has indicated

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:04.290
that his forces

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.659
will return to the front lines in August.

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:07.860
What more can you tell us

00:07:10.363 --> 00:07:12.598
Well, Yevgeny Prigozhin, the

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:15.868
mercurial leader of the Wagner

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:17.837
mercenary group, has indeed,

00:07:17.837 --> 00:07:18.304
as you rightly

00:07:18.304 --> 00:07:19.772
say, said that his troops

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:21.240
will be returning to the frontline

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:21.674
in August.

00:07:21.674 --> 00:07:23.409
They were fighting in parliament.

00:07:23.409 --> 00:07:24.977
Indeed, it was their rotation

00:07:24.977 --> 00:07:25.945
out in the rotation

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:28.114
of other regular Army groups,

00:07:28.114 --> 00:07:30.316
and that coincided with this Ukrainian

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:32.752
push and advances.

00:07:32.752 --> 00:07:34.220
But crucially,

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:34.954
he has said

00:07:34.954 --> 00:07:37.390
that he will not allow his troops,

00:07:37.957 --> 00:07:39.959
as others have agreed to do,

00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:40.760
in other militias

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.528
and other private military companies

00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:44.497
to sign contracts with Russia's

00:07:44.497 --> 00:07:46.165
Ministry of Defense,

00:07:46.165 --> 00:07:48.434
an organization that he has very loud

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:50.102
and very public contempt for.

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:51.471
How that resolves itself,

00:07:51.471 --> 00:07:53.339
I think we'll see play out

00:07:53.339 --> 00:07:54.707
over the next few weeks.

00:07:54.707 --> 00:07:56.943
But he has said he would

00:07:56.943 --> 00:07:58.177
return to the fray.

00:07:58.177 --> 00:07:58.711
So that,

00:07:58.711 --> 00:08:00.480
I suppose, from the Russian perspective,

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:01.514
might be a good thing.

00:08:01.514 --> 00:08:02.248
Although

00:08:02.482 --> 00:08:05.585
his men and his behavior often undermines

00:08:05.585 --> 00:08:07.820
the leadership structures, there

00:08:08.154 --> 00:08:09.555
for Ukraine.

00:08:09.555 --> 00:08:10.156
Linda,

00:08:10.189 --> 00:08:12.225
Sam Kiley for us in Kiev, Ukraine,

00:08:12.258 --> 00:08:13.259
good to have you across

00:08:13.259 --> 00:08:14.794
all those developments. Thanks so much.

